WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.324
These farms
run on water

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:02.821
from the last
Ice Age.

00:00:03.204 --> 00:00:05.944
In 1987,
this was empty desert.

00:00:06.269 --> 00:00:07.744
Then
the circles came.

00:00:08.127 --> 00:00:08.998
Each is a farm

00:00:09.044 --> 00:00:11.180
about a kilometer
wide, watered

00:00:11.215 --> 00:00:13.154
by a rotating
sprinkler arm.

00:00:13.595 --> 00:00:16.184
By 1992,
the desert kingdom

00:00:16.242 --> 00:00:17.531
was exporting
over two

00:00:17.624 --> 00:00:19.192
million tons
of wheat.

00:00:19.575 --> 00:00:20.550
The water
is pumped

00:00:20.597 --> 00:00:22.280
from deep
aquifers filled

00:00:22.315 --> 00:00:24.219
about twenty
thousand years ago.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.378
Rain here can't
refill them.

00:00:27.191 --> 00:00:28.515
In 2016,

00:00:28.665 --> 00:00:30.012
Saudi
Arabia ended

00:00:30.059 --> 00:00:32.427
its wheat program
to save water.

00:00:32.752 --> 00:00:33.867
Many farmers
switched

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:35.550
to alfalfa,
which uses

00:00:35.608 --> 00:00:37.002
three times
the water.

00:00:37.605 --> 00:00:39.440
That year,
hydrologists

00:00:39.521 --> 00:00:40.845
estimated
about fifty

00:00:40.926 --> 00:00:42.261
more years
of pumping.

00:00:42.505 --> 00:00:44.014
All of this,
built on water

00:00:44.061 --> 00:00:45.744
that doesn't
come back.
